  "details": "I realize \"favorites\" has been requested a million times - but I don't believe it goes far enough. This suggestion is different. \n\nA \"Worlds visited\" (linked to your hard disk cached worlds) list would be nice with an \"updated!\" marker on the ones that have recently been updated.\n\nThe ability to \"remove\" from the \"recently visited\" list would delete that world's cached instance from your disk. \n\nSince \"popular\" is right in the middle of your view way at the top - users are funneled there - intentionally or not. \n\nI imagine keeping up with \n\"featured\" is difficult. \n\nThere are so many environments that get ignored by the vast majority of the community and this may lead to boredom or a downtick in new but returning users - it's the same effect as mmorpgs experience - \"release hype\" followed by \"rush to endgame\" folks. Once they explore the top worlds, interact, find or make a personal avatar, interest wanes in those users until an expansion comes out.  You can hook people HARD by making sure the \"wow!\" effect is there every single day - you have enough content creators now to insure that. \n\nVRChat has no issues with new content, unlike mmorpgs. Even most streamers spend the majority of their time in default worlds at the moment - which is a shame for the success of the platform.\n\nI've had a TON of fun lately introducing people to Club Mechanix, Rave Robbi, Seaside, and a few of the more detailed and new worlds that have popped up - and it AMAZES me how few people scroll through new or world-hop. So many of them say that they go where people are, but they stand, jaw agape, at how nice some of these places are. \n\nEven somewhat elite advanced users I see online on a daily basis (with custom avatars and overrides) had no idea that places that beat the pants off (visually) to the \"big 5\" (mmd, void, pug, presentation, open mic) worlds now exist since they're always listed in order of popularity first, and new is wayyyy at the bottom. \n\nAlso an issue - simply updated worlds show up in \"new\" and override actually new worlds.",
